      "content": "No, you should not take a higher dose of ibuprofen or vitamins to treat a potential eye issue, as this can be dangerous and ineffective. While migraines do cause visual symptoms, the specific combination of flashes and new floaters is a classic warning sign for a retinal tear that almost always requires immediate medical attention, not home remedies. Since financial stress cannot be your excuse for waiting when vision loss is a risk, please find a way to get to an urgent care clinic or ophthalmologist today to save your eyesight.",
